        "summarize"
      ],
      "gpus": 4,
      "shm_size": "32gb"
    },
    {
      "id": "sim-auto-stage1-short-train",
      "prompt": "Run a short first run of Stage 1 (teacher forcing) of the Sim-Auto distillation for real on the four GPUs of this machine, on the shared daytime reference scene. Use the released nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto (a snapshot at a revision you pin and record) as the Transfer-Auto starting point: convert it to the weights-only initializer that Stage 1 starts from, package the scene's supplied training index (paragraph captions, seven cameras) into the local training bundle, select Stage 1 for a new chain with the run group sim_auto_stage1_short_train, apply the bundle camera-map overrides, the skill's smoke settings for a short first run and the short-window settings it gives for this 720p scene (two updates, a checkpoint saved at iteration 2), resolve the stage with a dry run at the CP4/FSDP4 topology of the skill's bounded check, and then launch it with the skill's stage launch command as one node with four processes. Carry the run as far as the skill requires of a bounded Stage 1 run before its checkpoint is accepted: finite losses, strict initialization and a completed save for the two updates, and then the skill's fresh-process resume check of the same stage. If the run does not fit this machine's GPU memory, say so with the error text and the measured memory, and do not present a reduced or partial run as the documented check. The matched RGB VAE that the Quickstart binds is Wan2.2_VAE.pth of Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B. The scene is not vendored in the skill: the documented workflow downloads it from the Transfer-Auto model repository on Hugging Face (nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto, assets/sample_data) and verifies its checksums; use that scene, no substitute media. Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill. Keep the training output root and every checkpoint, weight and model file outside the artifacts directory, and copy none of them into outputs/. Sample the used memory of every GPU with nvidia-smi every few seconds during each launch: start the sampler shortly before the launch so that its first rows show the GPUs before the processes start, stop it by its process id as soon as the launch ends, and collect the samples in outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/gpu_memory.csv. Save the complete console output (stdout and stderr) of the two-update launch, captured while it runs, as outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/train_log.txt and that of the resume launch, captured the same way, as outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/resume_log.txt, and when both are done write a listing of the checkpoints directory in the stage's output folder (every file below that directory, one path relative to the stage's output folder with its size in bytes per line) to outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/checkpoint_listing.txt. These three files are only for the two-update launch with exactly the settings and topology named above and for its resume check, also when one of them fails: if one fails, record the failure in result_summary.md before you try anything else, and give a launch with any changed training setting a run group of its own and output files of its own beside these three (names ending in _reduced), with every changed setting listed in result_summary.md. Record in result_summary.md the snapshot revision, the exact dry-run, launch and resume commands with their settings and topology, the wall-clock time of each launch, the loss printed for each iteration, and the peak memory of each of the four GPUs during each launch.",
      "expected_outcome": "The released Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto snapshot is converted to the weights-only initializer of Stage 1 (SIM_AUTO_STAGE0_CHECKPOINT), the daytime scene is packaged into the local training bundle, and Sim-Auto Stage 1 (experiment sim_auto_joint_stage1_tf_all, run group sim_auto_stage1_short_train, job stage1_seed0) is resolved with the bundle camera-map overrides, the smoke settings, the scene's short-window settings and the CP4/FSDP4 topology and then trained for real by torchrun with four processes: two updates with finite losses, strict initialization and a complete checkpoint saved synchronously at iteration 2, followed by a fresh-process resume of the same stage to iteration 3; the two console logs, the checkpoint listing and the GPU memory samples are under outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/ with no checkpoint or model file copied there, and result_summary.md records the commands, the wall-clock time of each launch, the loss of each iteration and the peak memory of each GPU.",
      "assertions": [
        "The Transfer-Auto snapshot (hf download nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto at a pinned, recorded revision) was converted by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.prepare_sim_auto_checkpoint with --checkpoint-path set to the snapshot and --output-path set to a new SIM_AUTO_STAGE0_CHECKPOINT directory; the local training bundle was built by cosmos_framework.data.generator.local_simulation.auto_bundle from the supplied training-index.jsonl of the daytime scene (downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Transfer-Auto assets/sample_data and verified against its SHA256SUMS) with the seven camera keys; and COSMOS_SIM_AUTO_LOCAL_BUNDLE, RGB_VAE, LIDAR_VAE, QWEN_TOKENIZER (the bundle's resources/tokenizer), IMAGINAIRE_OUTPUT_ROOT and SIM_AUTO_RUN_GROUP were bound as the Quickstart does",
        "Stage 1 was selected for a new chain (module stage1_tf, experiment sim_auto_joint_stage1_tf_all, job.group=sim_auto_stage1_short_train, job.name=stage1_seed0, checkpoint.keys_to_skip_loading=[net_ema.]) with the four bundle camera-map removals (camera_keys, camera_caption_key_mapping, camera_control_key_mapping, camera_sampler), the skill's smoke settings for a short first run (job.wandb_mode=disabled with the wandb, wandb_2x and wandb_val callbacks removed, trainer.callbacks.norm_monitor.log_stat_wandb=false, model.config.max_num_tokens_after_packing=100000, dataloader_train.max_sequence_length=100000, dataloader_train.max_samples_per_batch=1, model.config.compile.enabled=false, trainer.logging_iter=1, object-store loading and saving disabled, trainer.max_iter=2, checkpoint.save_iter=2, checkpoint.dcp_async_mode_enabled=false) and the scene's short-window overrides (the 480p stream removed, the 720p stream at ratio 1.0 with num_video_frames=24 and joint_aligned_num_video_frames=21), and was resolved before the launch by python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment --config cosmos_framework/configs/simulation/config.py --experiment-module cosmos_framework.configs.simulation.experiment.auto.stage1_tf --dryrun, from the framework environment with COSMOS_INTERNAL=0 and COSMOS_TRAINING=1 and without COSMOS_SMOKE, at model_parallel.context_parallel_size=4, model.config.parallelism.context_parallel_shard_degree=4 and model.config.parallelism.data_parallel_shard_degree=4",
        "Stage 1 was launched with the skill's stage launch command as one node with four processes (torchrun --nnodes=1 --nproc-per-node=4 --node-rank=0 --rdzv-backend=c10d with the rendezvous endpoint on port 29500 of this machine, -m cosmos_framework.scripts.train_experiment) with the same entry, settings and topology as that dry run, so four processes trained on the four GPUs at CP4/FSDP4 for exactly two updates and saved the checkpoint synchronously at iteration 2; outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/train_log.txt is the console output of that launch and shows the losses of iterations 1 and 2",
        "The run was carried to what the skill requires of a bounded Stage 1 run (finite loss, strict initialization and a completed synchronous save for the two updates, the checkpoint inventory, then the fresh-process resume check): the losses of both iterations are finite; the converted Transfer-Auto weights loaded strictly; the checkpoint of iteration 2 is complete (outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/checkpoint_listing.txt shows its model/, optim/, scheduler/ and trainer/ state, the loader state of the four ranks and latest_checkpoint.txt); and the same stage was then resumed in a fresh process under the same identity (job.group=sim_auto_stage1_short_train, job.name=stage1_seed0, same output root) with the EMA skip cleared (checkpoint.keys_to_skip_loading=[]) and the absolute endpoint 3 (trainer.max_iter=3), with outputs/sim_auto_stage1_short_train/resume_log.txt showing the iteration-2 checkpoint restored and iteration 3 made with a finite loss",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the two console logs, the checkpoint listing and the GPU memory samples trace to real commands in the transcript, no checkpoint, weight or model file was copied into outputs/, and result_summary.md records the snapshot revision, the commands, the wall-clock time of each launch, the loss printed for each iteration and the peak memory of each of the four GPUs as actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
